# A defect in my own first version of the finding-1 test, found and fixed before commit.
# The first final-round run (kiln r350) hit its 600 s timeout with no output (a `| tail -c` pipe held it);
# its last step log on the runner read "observer_sockets_are_checked_by_identity_beside_other_tests_descriptors
# has been running for over 60 seconds". That run was killed during mutation m01, which stayed applied in the
# runner's copy (kiln's sync sends local changes only), so the probe below ran with m01 in place.
# command (kiln r374): sh docs/research/measurements/audit-fix-tests-v1/logs/f01-hang-probe.sh 2>&1 | tail -c 25000
# Reading: the assertion failed (m01's blind check returns []) inside std::thread::scope, the neighbor thread
# then waited forever at its Barrier (futex_wait) and the scope waited for it: a failure became a hang.
# Fix: the test has no threads or barriers now (final-round.log: it fails promptly under m01), and every
# runner script first reverts a leftover mutation and checks the tree against the local diff (runner-prelude.sh).
